# Critical Review (claude, 2026-05-18)

Snapshot: `cargo test --workspace --locked` → **143 passed / 52 suites / 4.95 s**.
LOC by crate: core 1.0k, sig 1.2k, radar 2.1k, validate 2.4k, dataset 1.5k,
cli 0.6k, world 0.3k, studio 0.4k. 17 schemas, 5 fixture object cards,
1 scenario, 1 sensor archetype, 1 Monte-Carlo preset.

The scaffold is healthy. It is *not* yet a world-class dataset foundry.
Below are the concrete gaps a top-tier radar reviewer (or a serious open
dataset consumer) will hit on day one.

## A — Validation ladder is half-built (V0/V1/V2 only)
`docs/validation-tiers.md` admits V3-V5 are deferred. Promotion gates in
`crates/echoforge-validate/src/report.rs` only handle V0/V1/V2. Tip5 is
right that **method-ceiling (fidelity F0-F5)** and **evidence-tier
(validation V0-V6)** are distinct axes — today we conflate them into a
single `ValidationTier` enum. The 7-variant V0-V5 + 5-string-alias enum
in `crates/echoforge-core/src/models.rs` already drifts from the docs.

## B — Material card is one paragraph deep
`schemas/material_card.schema.json` requires scalar permittivity
(real, imag), one conductivity number, one roughness number, one
frequency range. Tips 2/5/6 all demand a **three-layer separation**:
physical-prior → solver-supported representation → surrogate correction.
Missing fields:
- `frequency_validity_hz` (currently `frequency_range_hz` but no
  validity-mask semantics)
- `solver_compatibility` map (e.g. `sagitta_sbr:
  effective_scatterer_or_pec_proxy`)
- `uncertainty_policy` block (sample_count_default,
  propagate_to_rcs_uncertainty, downgrade_confidence_if_unvalidated)
- material confidence grade
- thickness / layer stackup
- anisotropy flag
- loss tangent distribution (not just real/imag)

## C — Object pack roster is dangerously narrow
- **One** public-proxy object card: `public-proxy-uav-1` (generic fixed
  wing, dimensions 2.4 × 1.6 × 0.4 m).
- **Three** hard-negative cards: birds, commercial drones,
  terrain_weather.
- **One** sensor archetype: `baseline-x-band-fmcw`.
- **Zero** meshes, **zero** parametric geometry, **zero** trajectory
  generators.

Tip1 §11.2 / tip4 / tip5 expect at least 8 public-proxy families and a
hard-negative taxonomy of ~25 entries spread across biological,
civilian-benign, infrastructure, vehicles, environment, sensor
artifacts.

## D — Iranian-only demo concentration (the headline credibility risk) [SUPERSEDED 20260518T160000Z]
