# Cross-tip conflict resolutions (historical)

The seven proposals disagreed on six axes. The authoritative merge for
EchoForge was:

| Axis | Resolution | Rationale |
|---|---|---|
| Validation ladder depth | **V0–V6** validation tiers (evidence) + **F0–F5** fidelity classes (method ceiling), tracked as two independent fields. | Tip5's separation is the cleanest; conflating them is what produced the V0-V5/V0-V8 disagreement across tips. F = "how good can this method ever be", V = "how much evidence has this artifact accumulated". Renaming required: drop the 5-string-alias enum in `crates/echoforge-core/src/models.rs` once V3–V5 land. |
| Credibility grades | **Confidence labels A–E** (tip6). | Single-character alphabetic ordering is unambiguous in code and CSV. |
| Object ID naming | ~~Neutral generic IDs~~ → **Platform names allowed in default paths per user direction 20260518T160000Z.** Historical rule rejected. | Reversal of earlier tip2-rejection decision per user. |
| Difficulty tier count | **H0–H5** for hard negatives (tip1/2/6), with H5 = open-set held-out family. | Six levels covers the taxonomy without over-fragmenting. |
| Hard-negative package | **Keep folded inside `echoforge-world`** for now; split to `echoforge-hardneg` only when the mining loop crosses ~2k LOC. | YAGNI. |
| Phase count | **8 phases** (P0 foundation already done; P1 diversify+materials; P2 radar-chain depth; P3 solver adapters; P4 validation V3-V5; P5 hard-negative mining; P6 benchmark + ML baseline; P7 Studio traceability). | Matches tip5/6/7 and absorbs the existing P0 work. |
| EchoSig layout | **Keep the current Rust `EchosigBundleWriter` layout**. | Don't refactor a working bundle layout for hypothetical readers. |
| Stone Soup role | **Adapter + baseline tracker only**, never the canonical truth. | Tip2/5/6 agreement; tip3 over-scoped it. |
| RadarSimPy | **Optional, license-gated, never in strict-open default**. | Tip1/2/7 agreement; license is restrictive. |

